      "source": [
        "### Repaint a photo with only 8 colors\n",
        "\n",
        "Here's the trick. A photo is a big pile of pixels, and every pixel is a point in color\n",
        "space: (red, green, blue).\n",
        "\n",
        "Run K-Means on those points with `k=8` and you get the 8 colors that best represent the\n",
        "whole photo. Repaint every pixel with its group's color and you've built an **image\n",
        "compressor**."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "38a608ab",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 385
        },
        "id": "38a608ab",
        "outputId": "6f8e6950-577f-44b7-c4e0-a0af359e61ba"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Total pixels: 273280\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 600x400 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
        "from sklearn.datasets import load_sample_image\n",
        "\n",
        "photo = load_sample_image(\"flower.jpg\") / 255.0\n",
        "pixels = photo.reshape(-1, 3)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Total pixels:\", len(pixels))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(6, 4))\n",
        "plt.imshow(photo)\n",
        "plt.axis(\"off\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Original\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
